WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Treasure Island

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:10.950
<i>Silver was given the Black Spot
for saving my life.</i>

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.630
<i>That means that he's no longer a pirate.</i>

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.180
From now on, you're no longer our leader.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.460
What do you take me for, you filthy rats!

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:43.600
Silver, behind you!

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:44.900
Scum!

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.080
Silver!

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.220
Come on guys, tie him up!

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:15.950
Treasure
Island

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:15.750
Takarajima

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.560
saa ikou

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.560
Come, let's go

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.650
yume ni mita shima heto

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.650
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.490
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.490
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.370
umi hedeyou

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.370
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:37.290
ikute ni wa

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:37.290
Many of us

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:40.290
minna mada shiranai

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:40.290
Still don't know of

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:44.040
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:44.040
The days and nights full of mystery

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.540
matte iru darou

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.540
That await us there

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:50.050
itsumo shinji you

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:50.050
We must always have trust

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.300
magokoro wo

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.300
And be sincere

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:59.560
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:59.560
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.690
tade hitotsu no

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.690
I only...

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:06.110
akogare dake wa

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:06.110
...have one desire

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.400
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.400
And no one...

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:15.110
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:15.110
...will ever take it away

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.660
tade hitotsu no

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.660
I only...

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.960
akogare dake wa

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.960
...have one desire

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:27.290
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:27.290
And no one...

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:34.220
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:34.220
...will ever take it away

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:45.220
episode

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:45.220
This Time it's
\h  Long John's Crucifixion !

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.000
Hey, Silver!

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:03.200
I'm going to tell you why we've given you the black spot.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.660
The first reason is Jim.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.840
He keeps spoiling our plans!

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:16.080
I've lost count of all the dirty tricks he's played.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.110
And you've always protected him.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:23.100
He's right!
You've betrayed us all, Silver!

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:24.970
Yeah, that's right!

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.310
Dirty traitor!

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:33.600
Hey guys, why don't you use your heads for a bit?

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.530
I didn't know my men were so stupid!

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.560
You think I was protecting him?

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.750
How long have you been pirates?!

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.910
Jim is a valuable hostage.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:54.320
As long as he's with us,
we have nothing to fear.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:56.920
He's our trump card—the ace of spades.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:01.350
And you were about to kill such a valuable hostage?!

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.920
I see.
Impressive as ever, Silver...

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.400
Thanks for the valuable advice.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.940
Got it.
We'll have to keep Jim hostage.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.880
But you've fooled us long enough.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:19.650
The second reason you've received the spot...

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.200
...is for your incompetence.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.230
My incompetence?

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.520
Many of us have died.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:31.570
We're all that's left.
Additionally,

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.760
those that caught the fever will soon be dead!

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:40.440
Why didn't we get rid of those landlubbers in the first place?!

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:43.090
How will you take responsibility?
Tell us, Silver!

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:46.650
He's right!
You've deceived and used us!

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:49.650
You want to be the only one to reap the rewards!

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:51.060
Yeah, what he said!

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:51.060
Yeah, what he said!

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.360
What do you take me for?

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:59.570
Without me, you would never find the treasure!

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:02.190
You'd have died a long time ago!

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:06.160
Enough out of you.
That won't work on us anymore!

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:08.160
Prepare to die, scum!

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:12.690
However, it would be a shame to kill you quickly.

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:14.670
As is befitting of master Barbecue,

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:16.640
you'll be roasted alive by tomorrow!

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:18.960
Roasted?

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:23.330
Silver!

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:25.130
Come on, let's go, Jim!

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:25.680
Move.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:26.390
Silver!

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:28.970
Silver!

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:44.730
<i>Even if the lightning doesn't strike here,</i>

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:48.410
<i>he'll still have to spend the night in the rain...</i>

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:07.550
Silver!

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.550
Silver, Silver!

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:10.300
Hey, Jim.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:16.050
You know, even if he held up, he'd be more dead than alive.

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:19.730
After all, it was very cold last night.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:29.340
Hello, there you are.
Good morning, everyone.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:31.820
I slept very well!

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:33.740
<i>Silver!</i>

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:37.860
In fact, I slept extremely well up here.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:45.090
Just you wait! We'll do something about that smart mouth of yours!

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:45.590
Hurry!

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:55.570
You'll need your crutch to wander in hell.

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:57.770
I have pity.
Here.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:05.650
And don't worry about Flint's treasure.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:09.380
With this map we won't have any trouble finding it.

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:16.910
Now, say your prayers before hell greets you, Silver.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.540
Silver!

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:26.990
Mutineers to the gallows!
To the gallows!

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:30.310
George and Morgan have betrayed Silver!

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:32.050
Mutineers to the gallows!

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:34.050
George and Morgan are traitors!

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:35.140
Dirty beast...
Who are you calling traitors?!

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.880
George and Morgan to the gallows!

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:38.440
George and Morgan to the gallows!

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:43.150
To the gallows! To the gallows!
To the gallows!

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:49.110
Looks like Flint will tell other pirate ships passing the area about your treason.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:53.250
To us, you're the traitor!

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:55.070
The men are all with me.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:59.040
For me, the only traitor here is you.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:01.500
D-Damn you!
Morgan, set fire to the stake!

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.060
With pleasure!

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:04.460
Wait, Morgan.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:09.380
Before I burn in hell, there's one thing I've been wondering about...

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:13.260
Tell me, George. How do you expect to leave the island without me?

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.430
Who's going to navigate the ship?
You?

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:18.400
You don't have the experience.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:23.460
You should know very well that you
can't improvise when you're captain.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:27.950
You can't navigate the ship alone.

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:30.300
Even if you find the treasure,

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:34.090
you'll end up with the ship
at the bottom of the ocean.

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:36.070
The smallest storm will
send you to the bottom!

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:40.340
You want to die with the treasure?

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:43.290
Are you prepared to follow it to the bottom of the ocean?!

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:49.710
S-Silver!

00:08:54.420 --> 00:09:00.140
I-I... don't want to die of fever on this godforsaken island.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:02.100
Y-You and I are...

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:05.140
You see, I-I've always
put my life in your hands.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:09.140
Captain Silver, you're the only one who can find the treasure.

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:11.140
And you're the only one
who can get us out of here.

00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:14.300
Thanks, Anderson.
You're brave...

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:17.060
You've held on so far with the fever.

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:20.020
I know I can count on you.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.200
Hey, Giraffe!

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:24.940
He's very sick.
Bring him inside.

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:26.620
Huh? Oh, okay...

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:27.460
Hurry up!

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:28.330
Y-Yes.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:30.290
George...

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:34.840
Don't you know it's not very wise to rush in head first?

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.340
Especially when you want to become a leader.

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:38.220
Hey, Puppy!

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:42.310
Untie me.

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:48.640
I've spent the night on this cross.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:51.230
I might not be able to take the helm.

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:55.440
Understand, Puppy?

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:16.580
So guys, what's your decision?

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:20.310
You have two choices:
follow George and die,

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:25.680
or follow me and return home with the treasure!

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:26.270
What'll it be?!

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:30.400
Silver!

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.100
Yeah, Silver!

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:34.440
Yeah!
He's our captain!

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:36.440
Silver!

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:37.020
Yeah, Silver!

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:38.280
Who else but Silver?

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:39.070
Yes, Silver!

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:40.700
Hey, Puppy.

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:42.370
Y-Yes?

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:43.910
My crutch.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:45.310
Y-Yes.

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:12.100
Now, return the map to me.

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:23.060
You can stay on your side or follow us.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:24.240
Choose.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:29.260
You know George.
When you plan a mutiny,

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:33.760
you must have a plan or no one follows.

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:35.790
A little something to reflect upon.

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:43.720
Hey, Puppy.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.230
Y-Yes?

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:48.180
Untie Jim and Benbow.

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:49.640
Yes, right away.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:51.100
Silver...

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:55.060
Come on, Jim. Follow me.
We'll drink some good coffee.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:00.710
<i>I... don't know how to say this.</i>

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:02.600
<i>It may seem strange, but I...</i>

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:05.330
<i>...forgot that he was once our enemy.</i>

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:09.150
<i>I just wanted to throw myself
into his arms to thank him.</i>

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:25.510
Captain Silver, come quickly!
It's Anderson!

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:34.830
Come on, hold on.
Hold on, Anderson!

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:36.400
What can we do, captain?

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:38.630
Only Dr. Livesey can help him.

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:42.400
Someone, go and find Dr. Livesey quickly!

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:43.360
Silver.

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:46.540
I'll do it. Let me go, okay?

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:47.240
J-Jim?

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:51.710
Listen, Jim...

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:54.040
You're a valuable hostage to us.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.750
I have no intention of running away!

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.000
I'm going to bring you Dr. Livesey!

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:00.300
You swear it?

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:01.460
I swear!

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:05.130
I have your word as a man?

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:05.970
Yes.

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:08.430
Okay, show him the way!

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.570
<i>I wonder how they're doing.
I hope they're alright!</i>

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:17.500
<i>Why did they give Silver the map?</i>

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:20.430
<i>Were they defeated and gave up the treasure?</i>

00:13:20.430 --> 00:13:23.780
<i>I'll ask when I find them!</i>

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:29.910
Captain, what if he doesn't return?

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:32.230
George could start up again.

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:35.670
We'll see when that happens.
For now, we must trust Jim.

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:36.460
Captain!

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:44.860
Let's see...
It must be here.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.230
Ahoy!

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:50.680
Ahoy!

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:53.640
Hey, Jim, we're here!

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:56.600
Hey, Gray!

00:13:57.270 --> 00:14:00.270
Hey, everybody!
Jim is here! He's alive!

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:02.590
Really, is it Jim?

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:14.450
Oh, Jim!

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:17.040
You're safe and sound!
We were so worried!

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:17.960
Allow me.

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:20.750
You're all safe!

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:24.430
As you can see, we're fine.

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:27.710
But tell me, how did you find us?

00:14:27.710 --> 00:14:29.890
Silver told me were to find you.

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:31.850
Silver?

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.230
Oh, right!

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:40.190
Since I didn't know that you had left the fort,

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:43.190
I went back there and I was captured.

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:44.900
And you escaped?

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:47.990
No, I came to find you, Dr. Livesey.

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:51.030
Boatswain Anderson is very sick.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:54.030
You have to come with me to the fort.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:55.630
What's that?
Wait a minute, Jim.

00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:57.540
Silver sent you?

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:58.480
Yes, he did.

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:01.850
Hey Jim,  don't tell me
you're with the enemy...

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:05.750
Mr. Trelawney, how can you say that?!

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:08.010
Besides, who gave him the map, huh?!

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:10.310
Did you surrender and give up the treasure?!

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:15.720
Jim.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:18.910
We haven't surrendered.

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:20.690
Nor have we given up the treasure.

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:24.400
We have a good reason
for giving them the map.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:26.230
A-A good reason?

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.360
Jim!

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:30.700
Yes, we handed them the map,

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:38.290
because we knew that it wouldn't help them find the treasure.

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:41.520
It wouldn't help them?

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:46.310
When you left to cut the moorings of the ship,

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:48.630
a terrible storm arose.

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:50.870
All five of us were completely soaked.

00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:53.590
Of course, so was the map.

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:57.140
That's why I tried to dry it by the fireplace.

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:58.520
When suddenly,

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:01.440
I saw two small paragraphs appear.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:03.470
Imagine our surprise!

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:07.050
Who would have thought
they had used invisible ink?

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:10.550
The meaning of the text is very puzzling,

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:14.410
but I'm sure that it indicates the true location of the treasure.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:19.590
There, now you know everything.
And until you came back,

00:16:19.590 --> 00:16:23.370
we've been trying to solve this puzzle.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:26.630
I see!
It all makes sense now.

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.490
I feel reassured.

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:32.380
Silver hasn't beaten us yet.

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:38.060
Of course, Jim. They haven't heard the last of us yet!

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:40.850
The real battle is still to be fought.

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:42.020
He's right, Jim.

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:53.030
Come, Dr. Livesey.
You must come to the fort.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:56.030
Hurry.
Anderson is very sick.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.790
Hold it.
Wait a moment, Jim.

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:01.870
I'll go because I am a doctor and
because I gave my word to Silver,

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:04.000
but you don't have to go back.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:06.710
He's right, you're going to stay with us.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.950
It's not needed to go back there.

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:12.000
I, too, gave my word to Silver.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:13.510
I must go back.

00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:18.310
Giving your word to a pirate means nothing!

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:19.680
Mr. Trelawney.

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:23.640
Jim has given his word to Silver.

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:28.290
No matter what you say,
that man is still a pirate!

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:29.190
Curses!

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:30.630
Trelawney.

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:33.540
Don't you worry!
I'm just going to the bathroom.

00:17:37.270 --> 00:17:38.430
Jim.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:40.550
As the captain, I order you:

00:17:40.550 --> 00:17:43.330
Jim, return to the fort.

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:46.290
Yes, sir.

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:50.250
Know that I am proud to count you as one of us.

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:53.800
Return.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:54.710
Not return.

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:55.720
Return.

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:56.430
Not return.

00:17:57.740 --> 00:17:59.160
It's no use.

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:05.350
Anyway, he should be back by now.
What is he doing?

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:09.560
There he is!
He's here! He's here!

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:13.230
Captain Silver!
Jim has returned with Livesey!

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:20.380
Jim, don't tell them anything about the secret paragraphs.

00:18:20.380 --> 00:18:21.490
Can you promise me that?

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:22.600
Yes, absolutely.

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:51.590
Dr. Livesey, thank you for coming.

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:54.360
What do you say to one of Silver's "special coffees"?

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:55.940
No, thank you.

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:59.330
You're missing out.
Well, allow me to partake.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:04.160
So, how's Anderson?

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:07.070
I've given him medicine to help with the fever,

00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:09.120
but honestly, it's out of my hands.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:10.420
I get the picture.

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:13.910
You know, doctor,
Anderson is an old friend of mine.

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:15.340
If that's how it is...

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:19.760
I guess I'll have to find it quickly
if I want him to see the treasure...

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:26.020
But thank you, Dr. Livesey.
You came like you promised.

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:33.210
Dr. Livesey, I've decided to give
you a present by way of thanks.

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:37.670
You can leave your cave.

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:41.270
Go where you please.
I've given you your freedom.

00:19:41.270 --> 00:19:44.570
Our conditional truce stops here.

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:52.470
I'm sure that you've memorized the map.

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:55.880
From now on, may the best man win.

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:02.090
I understand, Silver.
I'll tell the others.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:05.050
Well, let's go, Jim.
It's time to leave.

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:08.140
One moment, Dr. Livesey.

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:13.300
He stays with me.
Jim is my last trump card.

00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:15.560
I'm keeping him hostage.

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:24.240
Don't look at me like that.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.950
In exchange, please accept this present.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:27.870
Hey, Puppy!

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:28.490
Yes?

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:31.460
Give Dr. Livesey back their weapons.

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:32.910
Here, take it.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:43.220
Jim, be patient. I will return with the others to free you.

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:59.980
Come, mates!
To the treasure!

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.750
Aye!

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:07.000
The sick, the wounded...
Bring them all with us!

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:07.950
Every single one.

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:09.870
I want everybody to be there
when we find the treasure!

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:17.170
Find the treasure! Go! Go!
Find the treasure! Find the treasure!

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:19.930
Fifteen men...

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:23.380
...on a dead man's chest!

00:21:24.060 --> 00:21:28.900
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum!

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:35.140
Drink and the devil
had done for the rest...

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:39.910
Yo-ho-ho!
...and another bottle of rum!

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:45.560
Okay, let's get started.

00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:48.530
Before anything, we must free Jim.

00:21:49.480 --> 00:21:50.950
Go, depart!

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:07.260
O treasure! You who sleep in the depths of darkness!

00:22:07.760 --> 00:22:10.720
Inundate us with your light!

00:22:10.880 --> 00:22:15.750
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum!

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:18.190
Drink and the devil...

00:22:18.190 --> 00:22:22.350
...had done for the rest!

00:22:22.350 --> 00:22:26.870
Yo-ho-ho!
...and another bottle of rum!

00:22:29.140 --> 00:22:32.630
To      be        continued

